course: dictionary
lesson: 15658
title: A thesis is the big idea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A thesis is the main idea that a writer wants to prove. In an essay, it is often one sentence that tells the reader what the essay will argue. «My thesis is that dogs make better pets than cats.» The writer then uses reasons and examples to show that this idea is true.
explain: The word thesis can also mean a very long piece of writing. Students at university write one at the end of their studies, based on research they have done themselves. Some students spend years on a thesis, which is why it is so long.
explain: Look for clues in the words around it. Words like «argue», «prove» and «claim» often sit near a thesis. Ask yourself: what is the writer trying to show? If you can answer that in one sentence, you have found the thesis.
fact: A thesis is the main idea or claim that a writer wants to prove.
fact: A thesis statement is one sentence that tells the reader what an essay will argue.
fact: A thesis is also a long piece of research writing, written for a university degree such as a PhD.
fact: The plural of thesis is theses.
fact: «To support a thesis» means to give reasons and evidence that show the main idea is true.
exercise: «My thesis is that school should start later.» What is the writer's thesis? | School is closed on Sundays | *School should start later | The writer is very tired | Later is a time of day
exercise: Maya is writing an essay. Which sentence is a thesis statement? | *Video games can help children learn maths | Yesterday it rained all afternoon | Today I went to the park with my dog | The park has three big swings
exercise: Which word means a long piece of research writing for a university degree? | puzzle | whisper | garden | *thesis
test: «To support a thesis, a writer gives reasons and examples.» What does support a thesis mean? | Write the thesis in red pen | Forget the main idea and start again | Read the thesis out loud to a friend | *Give reasons and examples that show the main idea is true
test: Ella's older sister is writing a PhD thesis. What is it? | A type of cake | A short shopping list | *A long piece of research writing for a university degree | A kind of bird
exam: Jamie writes: «My thesis is that reading every day makes you a better writer.» What is Jamie's main idea? | Writers are always busy people | Summer days are very long | *Reading every day makes you a better writer | Jamie likes reading books in the library
